(*"qualifications_schema.qualification"
A **qualification** is a particular instance of the formal identification of a capability or aptitude in a specific person or organization.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.__example"
John Smith's driving licence.
*)
(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.__example"
Mary Brown's doctorate entitled "Datamodelling Using EXPRESS2".
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.__note"
A relationship between a <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> object and one or more *qualification* objects is established by the declaration of a <<express:management_resources_schema.qualification_type_assignment,qualification_type_assignment>> subtype containing a single attribute that references a set of a SELECT type that contains an qualification.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **qualification** is known.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **qualification**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship"
A **qualification_relationship** is a relationship between two instances of the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> entity data type and provides for the identification, naming, and description of that relationship.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.description"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.text,text>> that characterizes the **qualification_relationship**. The value of this attribute need not be specified.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification_relationship**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.name"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.label,label>> by which the **qualification_relationship** is known
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.related_qualification"
the other instance of <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that is a part of the relationship. If one element of the relationship is dependent upon the other, this attribute shall be the dependent one.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.related_qualification.__note"
the meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.relating_qualification"
one of the instances of <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that is a part of the relationship.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.relating_qualification.__note"
The meaning of this attribute can be defined in the annotated EXPRESS schemas that use or specialize this entity, or in an agreement of common understanding between the partners sharing this information.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type"
An **qualification_type** is the formal identification of a capability or aptitude.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.__example"
A driving licence.
*)
(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.__example"
A university degree.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.__note"
A relationship between a *qualification_type* object and one or more <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> objects is established by the declaration of an <<express:management_resources_schema.qualification_type_assignment,qualification_type_assignment>> subtype containing a single attribute that references a set of a SELECT type that contains a <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>>.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.id"
the <<express:support_resource_schema.identifier,identifier>> that distinguishes the **qualification_type**.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.qualification_type.name"
