(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship"
The **acyclic_qualification_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.relatives"
(input) the set of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification,qualification>> that the function is searching for in the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship.relating_qualification,relating_qualification>> parameter of the **relation** argument.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_relationship.specific_relation"
(input) the fully qualified name of a subtype of the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_relationship,qualification_relationship>> entity.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship"
The **acyclic_qualification_type_relationship** function determines whether the graph of instances of the entity data type <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type,qualification_type>> that contains relation as one of its links contains a cycle. This function may be used to evaluate either an <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> or any of its subtypes.

The function returns TRUE if no cycle has been detected. Otherwise it returns FALSE.
*)


(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.__note"
The algorithm of the function is explained in annex E.2.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.__note"
This function is not used in this schema. It is defined here because other ISO 10303 integrated resources and application protocols that use the <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> entity include rules that use this function.
*)

(*"qualifications_schema.acyclic_qualification_type_relationship.relation"
(input) the candidate <<express:qualifications_schema.qualification_type_relationship,qualification_type_relationship>> to be checked.
*)


